  "subject": "english-language-arts",
  "summary": "A semester of ninth-grade English built around one idea, the threshold: argument, coming-of-age short fiction, poems by Robert Frost and Emily Dickinson, Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet, seminal U.S. documents that answer the Declaration of Independence (with a short research brief), and a personal essay. Six units, each with a student overview, a teacher guide with a five-day plan, a lesson, assignments, an assessment with a rubric and an answer key.",
  "title": "English 9",
  "version": "1.0.1"
